File Upload in Spring Boot (Step-by-Step) :

1. Create a Spring Boot Project
Create a new Spring Boot project.
Add dependencies:
Spring Web
(Optional) Lombok

2. Configure application.properties
Set the maximum file size.
Set the maximum request size.
(Optional) Specify the upload folder path.
Example:
spring.servlet.multipart.max-file-size=10MB
spring.servlet.multipart.max-request-size=10MB
file.upload-dir=uploads/

3. Create Upload Folder
Create a folder (e.g., uploads) in your project or specify any local path.

4. Create Service Interface
Add a method:
uploadFile(MultipartFile file)

5. Create Service Implementation
Receive the MultipartFile.
Get the original filename.
Save the file using Files.copy() or file.transferTo().
Return success message.

6. Create Controller
Create a POST API.
Use @RequestParam("file") MultipartFile file.
Call the service method.
Return response.

7. Test in Postman
Select POST request.
Choose Body → form-data.
Key:
file (Type = File)
Select a file.
Click Send.
Verify the file is stored in the upload folder.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
File Download in Spring Boot (Step-by-Step)

1. Create Service Interface
Add a method:
downloadFile(String fileName)

2. Create Service Implementation
Locate the file from the upload folder.
Convert it into a Resource.
Return the Resource.

3. Create Controller
Create a GET API.
Accept filename using @PathVariable or @RequestParam.
Call service method.
Set response headers:
Content-Disposition
Content-Type
Return ResponseEntity<Resource>.

4. Test in Browser/Postman
Open:http://localhost:8080/download/filename.pdf
OR send a GET request in Postman.
Browser/Postman downloads the file automatically.
